The third section discusses the prediction behavior of ALSH-approx in DNNs, noting its limitations when dealing with deep networks and class imbalance issues. It also introduces MC-approx as an alternative that performs well under certain conditions but has trade-offs such as increased training time and overfitting risks for deeper networks.

